594	// app/Sources/GraphicPreviewPlayer.swift — the Insert ▸ Graphic… sheet's
595	// looping preview (spec §11 G-45): one graphic module drawn frame after
596	// frame on a thread of its own, each frame handed to main as a `CGImage`.
597	//
598	// **One Foundation `Thread` per player, 8 MiB of stack**
599	// (`GraphicPrefetch.workerStackBytes`): QuickJS needs the deep stack, which
600	// a GCD thread does not have. The thread waits on an `NSCondition` while
601	// there is nothing to play, draws the subject's frame ⌊elapsed × fps⌋ mod
602	// its length, and waits until the next frame is due — a frame that took
603	// longer than one frame is followed by the frame due NOW, so a slow graphic
604	// skips rather than drifts. `stop()` ends the thread; nothing restarts it.
605	//
606	// **The thread touches no AppKit and no document.** Everything it reads is
607	// handed to it in `play`: the module (which holds its library, so the
608	// document's rescans cannot pull it away), its name and `meta`, and the
609	// canvas captured at init. A frame is delivered by a main hop, and only
610	// while its subject is still the newest one and the player has not stopped.
611	//
612	// **The picture is `render_graphic`'s**: the ctx is `AgentServer.graphicContext`
613	// at the module's size (`meta` width and height, else the canvas), with
614	// `props` `{}` — the schema's defaults — at `GraphicRegistry.previewBudgetMs`,
615	// composited over the contact sheet's checker
616	// (`GraphicContactSheet.paintChecker`). A frame that throws, and a module
617	// that does not compile, is the error card (`LayerRenderers.errorCardText`,
618	// `paintErrorCard`).
