1	// app/Sources/GraphicStore.swift — one document's `graphics/` folder: where
2	// it is, what is in it, and when that changes (road map 10 §5f, G3a). It
3	// scans, hashes (G-13) and says what changed; a file edit is not undo (G-3).
4	//
5	// **Created on the app's first write, never at open** (spec §11 G-14):
6	// `ensureFolder()` is the one creator inside a package; while it is absent
7	// the PACKAGE directory is watched, so an outside `mkdir` is seen.
8	//
9	// **The watch** is G0's q7(c): a folder source raises `.write` only and an
10	// in-place (`O_TRUNC`) save raises nothing on the folder, so each module,
11	// font and asset file up to `fileSourceLimit`, modules first (spec §11
12	// G-19 (c), G-20 (a)), has its own source; events are coalesced over 100 ms.
13	// Every pass re-opens every source BY PATH (a save swaps inodes) and arms
14	// BEFORE it scans. A source whose `open` fails is a scan warning (G-20 (b)).
15	// An illegal asset name is warned and skipped; fonts are `+Fonts`' (G-23).
16	//
17	// **Threading.** One serial queue alone touches the queue-confined state; it
18	// diffs, and main publishes in order through `drain()`. Main waits on the
19	// queue only through `queue.sync`; the queue never waits on main.
